      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:40:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): the program sim, setup sheet, tool list and cutting data know a tool-less wire cut\n\nA Wire Contour mounts no library tool (#532), so its Operation::tool is\nthe empty word. Each reader now asks KindInfo::mounts_tool():\n\n- program stock sim: plan_program leaves the wire cut out of the plan\n  (like the probe and torch), and simulate_document refuses the verdict\n  by name (\"a wire cut is verified by the wire laws, not the stock\n  sim\") instead of \"tool  is not in the library\"\n- setup sheet: the TOOL cell is \"cond <id>\", with the condition, wire\n  diameter and gap the machine states under the row; no missing-tool line\n- tool list and export: no row for the empty tool\n- cutting data: refuses by name that a wire cut mounts no library tool\n\nA milling op whose tool is gone is refused or listed exactly as before.\nPinned by crates/app/tests/wire_readers.rs.\n\nFixes #1110\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
